---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Telestar Corporation"
  description="Privacy policy and data governance practices of Telestar Corporation. How we collect, handle, and protect your communications data with zero third-party monetization."
>
  <div class="bg-slate-50 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center text-xs font-medium text-slate-500 mb-6 space-x-2">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-cyan-dark transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-slate-800">Privacy Policy</span>
      </nav>

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-8 mb-10">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Telestar Corporation ("Telestar", "we", "our", or "us") is dedicated to protecting the privacy, confidentiality, and security of our subscribers, their businesses, and their callers.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-400">
          Effective Date: September 2026
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Principle Callout -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-brand-cyan-light/50 border border-brand-cyan/20 text-slate-900 mb-10 space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-base text-brand-cyan-dark">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-cyan-dark flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
          Our Core Privacy Commitment
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          We operate as a telecommunications and cloud communication partner, not a data broker. <strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information, communications data, or caller metadata to third-party advertisers.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Document Body -->
      <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>
            In the course of providing hosted PBX, unified voice, video conferencing, and cloud backup services, Telestar collects the following categories of information:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>
              <strong>Account &amp; Subscriber Details:</strong> Business name, primary contact name, billing and physical service addresses, corporate email addresses, and phone numbers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Service Configuration &amp; E911 Records:</strong> Extension mappings, registered physical street addresses for emergency E911 dispatch, hunt group configurations, and automated attendant prompts.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Call Detail Records (CDR):</strong> Transactional metadata necessary to route calls and bill telecommunications services (originating phone number, destination phone number, timestamp, call duration, and transmission quality metrics).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Customer Communications:</strong> Support tickets, emails, and consultation inquiry details sent to our engineering team.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p>We use subscriber information solely for legitimate operational and statutory business purposes:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>To provision, maintain, route, and troubleshoot your voice, PBX, and collaboration services.</li>
            <li>To register and update E911 emergency dispatch physical locations with certified public safety routing gateways.</li>
            <li>To bill for telecom usage, long distance, and subscription seats.</li>
            <li>To respond to your support and customer service inquiries.</li>
            <li>To monitor network health and detect unauthorized or fraudulent telephone activity (e.g. international toll fraud).</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Customer Proprietary Network Information (CPNI)</h2>
          <p>
            Under federal telecommunications law, Call Detail Records and certain calling metadata constitute <strong>Customer Proprietary Network Information (CPNI)</strong>. Telestar strictly safeguards CPNI in accordance with FCC regulations. We require positive subscriber authentication before disclosing account call records, and we do not disclose CPNI to outside parties except as legally required or authorized by you.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Sharing with Service Partners</h2>
          <p>
            To deliver interconnected telecommunications, we partner with licensed upstream carrier networks and cloud infrastructure partners (such as Intermedia / Elevate and Cloudflare). These providers process data strictly as necessary to execute call switching, transit data packets, and store encrypted backups under strict confidentiality obligations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Data Security</h2>
          <p>
            We implement industry-standard physical, technical, and administrative safeguards to protect your data from unauthorized access, loss, or alteration. All web portal communications utilize Transport Layer Security (TLS 1.3), and platform assets are hosted on enterprise edge networks.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">6. Contacting Our Privacy Team</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or wish to review the personal data associated with your account, please reach out to:
          </p>
          <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-1 text-sm">
            <p><strong>Telestar Corporation</strong></p>
            <p>Attn: Privacy &amp; Compliance Office</p>
            <p>Telephone: <a href="tel:+18049308400" class="text-brand-cyan-dark font-semibold hover:underline">(804) 930-8400</a></p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@telestarcorp.com" class="text-brand-cyan-dark font-semibold hover:underline">support@telestarcorp.com</a></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
